data: {"type": "assistant_msg", "ts": "2026-08-06T12:22:10.024459+00:00", "content": "**Investigation Summary \u2013 `ce_branch24`**  \n\n**1. Hardware health** \u2013 All physical sensors read within normal ranges: fan 3000 RPM, power 72.5 W, PSU voltage 11.88 V, temperature 29 \u00b0C [metrics:0][metrics:1][metrics:2][metrics:3].\n\n**2. Local interfaces**  \n- **eth0 (WAN uplink)**: heavy throughput (9.9 MB in / 3.8 MB out) but **90 queue drops** and **1 877 inbound discards** \u2013 indicates congestion or policing on the provider edge [metrics:6][metrics:8][metrics:17][metrics:26].  \n- **eth1 (secondary WAN?)**: light traffic, only 2 queue drops, no discards [metrics:7][metrics:9][metrics:18].  \n- **eth2\u2013eth4 & VRFs**: low volume; VRFs *CORP* and *VOICE* show inbound counters but **zero outbound bytes** \u2013 possible asymmetric routing or policy block [metrics:14][metrics:15][metrics:23][metrics:24].\n\n**3. SD-WAN tunnels (6 hubs)** \u2013 All six tunnels are **up** (active path = 1 in topology [topo:ce_branch24]).  \n- **Latency**: 63\u201373 ms across hubs (best: ce_hub2 63 ms, worst: ce_hub1 73 ms) [metrics:6-11].  \n- **Jitter**: 1.3\u20138.1 ms (ce_hub2 best, ce_hub5/6 highest) [metrics:0-5].  \n- **Loss**: 0.02 %\u20130.94 %; **ce_hub1 tunnel shows near-1 % loss** and only 5 rekeys, while **ce_hub2 has 21 rekeys** despite low loss (0.18 %) \u2013 suggests intermittent instability on the ce_hub2 path [metrics:12-19].\n\n**4. Upstream / blast-radius** \u2013 One hop upstream is **pe12** (provider edge): BGP established (2 peers), MPLS LDP up, OSPF adjacencies full, 113 LSPs, no errors [topo:pe12]. Two downstream branch peers (`ce_branch12`, `p23`, `p24`) all report healthy tunnels and hardware [topo:ce_branch12][topo:p23][topo:p24].\n\n**5. Logs / flows / historical context** \u2013 No log lines returned for the investigation window [search_logs: none]; no flow records [flows: none]. Runbook and incident KB backends were unavailable, so no matched runbooks or prior incidents could be retrieved.\n\n---\n\n**Key findings / recommended actions**  \n1. **Investigate eth0 congestion** \u2013 90 queue drops + 1.9 k discards on the primary WAN uplink; engage provider (pe12) to verify policing / shaping on the CE-PE link.  \n2. **Monitor ce_hub1 tunnel** \u2013 Highest loss (0.94 %) with low rekey count; check path MTU, firewall timeouts, or ISP middlebox on that specific path.  \n3. **Review ce_hub2 rekeys** \u2013 21 rekeys may indicate flapping IKE/IPsec; inspect tunnel logs on both ends (not available here).  \n4. **Validate VRF egress policy** \u2013 CORP/VOICE VRFs receive traffic but send none; confirm route-leaking / firewall rules on `ce_branch24`.  \n5. **No log-based instructions found** \u2013 Since `search_logs` returned zero rows, there were no log-embedded instructions to follow.\n\n*All device-specific claims above are tied to the cited evidence IDs.*"}

